            "key_investigations.1",
            "treatment.0",
            "treatment.1",
            "treatment.2",
            "treatment.3",
            "treatment.4",
            "treatment.5"
          ],
          "text": "On admission, blood glucose was 'HI' on BM meter, blood ketones 5.2, pH 7.18, bicarbonate 11, and glucose 34. The DKA protocol was commenced with cautious IV fluids, fixed-rate insulin infusion, potassium replacement, and hourly monitoring; PICU was informed and the patient was managed on the ward HDU. By Day 2, pH had improved to 7.34 with ketones 0.8, and she was transitioned to subcutaneous insulin on a basal-bolus regimen. Diabetes nurse and dietician input was initiated, with structured family education covering carbohydrate counting, hypo management, and sick-day rules.",
          "unverified_fact_ids": []
        },
